                    <span class="railcard__meta"><span class="railcard__name">Gift sets</span><span class="railcard__n">7</span></span>
                </a>
                <a class="railcard" href="shop.html">
                    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470058869958-2a77ade41c02?w=340&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                         alt="" width="340" height="340" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
                    <span class="railcard__meta"><span class="railcard__name">Outdoor</span><span
                            class="railcard__n">15</span></span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="wrap section--tight" aria-labelledby="week-h">
            <div class="sechead">
                <div>
                    <p class="label">Potted this week</p>
                    <h1 id="week-h">Fresh from the polytunnel</h1>
                    <p>Everything below was potted on in the last seven days and is ready to travel.</p>
                </div>
                <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="shop.html">Shop all 10 plants</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <article class="band" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-7)">
            <div class="grid grid--2" style="align-items:center;gap:var(--s-6)">
                <div>
                    <p class="label">Start here</p>
                    <h2 style="margin:var(--s-3) 0 var(--s-4)">Almost every houseplant dies of kindness</h2>
                    <p style="margin-bottom:var(--s-4);max-width:48ch">
                        Overwatering outnumbers every other cause of death we see, by a long way. A plant
                        that is thirsty tells you within a day and recovers within two. A plant sitting in
                        wet compost tells you nothing for three weeks and then cannot be saved.
                    </p>
                    <p style="margin-bottom:var(--s-5);max-width:48ch">
                        Push a finger in to the second knuckle. If it comes out with compost stuck to it,
                        wait. That single habit will keep more plants alive than any feed or gadget.
                    </p>
                    <a class="btn btn--ochre" href="shop.html">Shop forgiving plants</a>
                </div>
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1416879595882-3373a0480b5b?w=900&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="A scoop of potting compost on a workbench" width="900" height="600"
                     style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--r-lg)" loading="lazy"
                     decoding="async"/>
            </div>
        </article>

        <div class="grid grid--3">
            <a class="guide" href="care.html">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1521334884684-d80222895322?w=700&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="Houseplants on a shelf beside a window" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy"
                     decoding="async"/>
                <div class="guide__meta"><span class="label">Light</span><span class="label">4 min read</span></div>
                <h3>Reading the light in your own rooms</h3>
                <p class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-sm)">"Bright indirect" is meaningless until you measure it.
                    Here is how, using the phone in your pocket.</p>
            </a>
            <a class="guide" href="care.html" style="--delay:80ms">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1416879595882-3373a0480b5b?w=700&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="Potting compost and a scoop" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
                <div class="guide__meta"><span class="label">Repotting</span><span class="label">6 min read</span></div>
                <h3>When a plant has outgrown its pot</h3>
                <p class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-sm)">Roots at the drainage hole are the obvious sign. Three
                    less obvious ones matter more.</p>
            </a>
            <a class="guide" href="care.html" style="--delay:160ms">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1602923668104-8f9e03e77e62?w=700&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="Patterned calathea foliage" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
                <div class="guide__meta"><span class="label">Diagnosis</span><span class="label">7 min read</span></div>
                <h3>What brown leaf tips are actually telling you</h3>
                <p class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-sm)">Usually not humidity. Four likelier explanations,
                    ordered by how often we see them.</p>
            </a>
            <a class="guide" href="care.html">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470058869958-2a77ade41c02?w=700&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="Dense glasshouse planting" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
                <div class="guide__meta"><span class="label">Winter</span><span class="label">5 min read</span></div>
                <h3>Getting a collection through a British winter</h3>
                <p class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-sm)">Less water, no feed, and move everything away from the
                    radiator — not towards it.</p>
            </a>
            <a class="guide" href="care.html" style="--delay:80ms">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485955900006-10f4d324d411?w=700&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="A small succulent in a pale pot" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
                <div class="guide__meta"><span class="label">Succulents</span><span class="label">4 min read</span>
                </div>
                <h3>Succulents want less than you think</h3>
                <p class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-sm)">Fortnightly in summer, monthly in winter, and gritty
                    compost. That is the whole method.</p>
            </a>
            <a class="guide" href="care.html" style="--delay:160ms">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512428813834-c702c7702b78?w=700&q=72&auto=format&fit=crop"
                     alt="A ginseng ficus bonsai" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
                <div class="guide__meta"><span class="label">Bonsai</span><span class="label">9 min read</span></div>
                <h3>A first year with a ficus bonsai</h3>
                <p class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-sm)">Do not prune it in month one. Do not repot it in month
                    two. Mostly, leave it alone.</p>
            </a>
        </div>

    </main>

{{/partial}}

